WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.201 --> 00:00:01.655
- Little ones!

00:00:01.655 --> 00:00:04.750
Yeah, oh my god, I want them all (laughs).

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:06.233
Hi little guy.

00:00:06.233 --> 00:00:07.747
Hello.

00:00:07.747 --> 00:00:10.473
I'm dying, I can't even
concentrate on what you're saying.

00:00:10.473 --> 00:00:12.973
(light music)

00:00:16.629 --> 00:00:19.212
(Emma squeals)

00:00:23.849 --> 00:00:27.978
I'm here with BuzzFeed, I'm
playing with tiny cute kittens.

00:00:27.978 --> 00:00:29.228
My day is made.

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:34.753
We designed for Belle this
ring that would sit on

00:00:34.753 --> 00:00:35.861
her little finger.

00:00:35.861 --> 00:00:37.603
The costume designer saw
that I had one which my mom

00:00:37.603 --> 00:00:40.627
had given to me, and she
was like, can I design

00:00:40.627 --> 00:00:41.475
one for Belle?

00:00:41.475 --> 00:00:43.801
Because Belle's mother dies
when she's really young.

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:45.450
My mom is still alive
and healthy and well,

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:46.327
just as a side-note.

00:00:46.327 --> 00:00:48.233
Anyway, I was really proud
of the ring and thought it

00:00:48.233 --> 00:00:50.139
was so beautiful that I
asked if I could keep one,

00:00:50.139 --> 00:00:51.491
and they said I could.

00:00:51.491 --> 00:00:52.740
Do you want to come down?

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.671
Is this a little high for you?

00:00:54.671 --> 00:00:56.344
Oh no, you kind of want to stay.

00:00:56.344 --> 00:00:59.570
Okay, you go here, you stay there,

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:02.123
and you can come down here.

00:01:02.123 --> 00:01:04.538
(upbeat music)

00:01:04.538 --> 00:01:07.162
I just wanted to make
sure that we stayed true

00:01:07.162 --> 00:01:09.306
to the original.

00:01:09.306 --> 00:01:11.704
So when Kevin Kline was
gonna make Maurice less

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.732
kind of like the inventor,
and he wasn't gonna have

00:01:13.732 --> 00:01:16.202
that as his story anymore,
I was like well could we

00:01:16.202 --> 00:01:17.441
use that for Belle?

00:01:17.441 --> 00:01:20.628
And so we made Belle this
inventor who invents this

00:01:20.628 --> 00:01:23.313
washing machine, so that
she can sit and read

00:01:23.313 --> 00:01:24.910
while it's doing her washing.

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:27.037
This one's chasing its
own shadow, literally.

00:01:27.037 --> 00:01:28.972
This is too much.

00:01:28.972 --> 00:01:31.472
(light music)

00:01:32.575 --> 00:01:35.505
I would want her to
know that she is a force

00:01:35.505 --> 00:01:39.343
to be reckoned with and,
never to underestimate

00:01:39.343 --> 00:01:41.066
her own power.

00:01:41.066 --> 00:01:43.895
Sometimes particularly
young girls feel like their

00:01:43.895 --> 00:01:45.597
voice doesn't matter,
and what they have to say

00:01:45.597 --> 00:01:48.094
doesn't really matter
and, I think I would want

00:01:48.094 --> 00:01:49.880
her to know that it does.

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:53.526
Oh, look at the rose pedals, look.

00:01:53.526 --> 00:01:55.051
Pretty rose pedals.

00:01:55.051 --> 00:01:57.551
(light music)

00:01:58.821 --> 00:02:00.043
So many times.

00:02:00.043 --> 00:02:03.092
When people have told me
that I can't do something,

00:02:03.092 --> 00:02:05.238
it's gonna be too hard, or whatever else,

00:02:05.238 --> 00:02:07.846
I try to use that as motivation.

00:02:07.846 --> 00:02:09.463
Sometimes someone telling
you that you won't

00:02:09.463 --> 00:02:10.324
be able to do something.

00:02:10.324 --> 00:02:11.768
I'm like oh you don't
know what you just did.

00:02:11.768 --> 00:02:14.263
Oh it's its shadow again.

00:02:14.263 --> 00:02:15.369
Too cute.

00:02:15.369 --> 00:02:18.341
(light music)

00:02:18.341 --> 00:02:21.843
In my imagining, she opens
the library that's in

00:02:21.843 --> 00:02:24.262
the castle, and she
turns it into a school,

00:02:24.262 --> 00:02:26.614
and a public library, which she runs.

00:02:26.614 --> 00:02:28.256
I love that all of these
guys are crazy and this one

00:02:28.256 --> 00:02:30.020
is just chill.

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:32.288
(light music)

00:02:32.288 --> 00:02:34.436
Yes, they share the love of books.

00:02:34.436 --> 00:02:38.946
Hermione and Belle are like
perfect head and heart girls.

00:02:38.946 --> 00:02:39.864
They have both.

00:02:39.864 --> 00:02:42.374
They're super smart, but they
also have this incredible

00:02:42.374 --> 00:02:46.214
empathy, and compassion,
and ability to see

00:02:46.214 --> 00:02:48.782
kind of beyond things,
and be non-judgemental.

00:02:48.782 --> 00:02:51.282
(light music)

00:02:52.426 --> 00:02:55.294
When we completed the final
dance at the end of the movie,

00:02:55.294 --> 00:02:59.734
I had the sound guys play
Happy, and Kevin Kline

00:02:59.734 --> 00:03:02.566
started doing the conga,
and like everyone joined in.

00:03:02.566 --> 00:03:04.324
It was the most surreal
thing I've ever seen.

00:03:04.324 --> 00:03:06.944
Everyone in costume, in the
Beauty and the Beast ballroom,

00:03:06.944 --> 00:03:08.173
doing the conga.

00:03:08.173 --> 00:03:11.116
(light music)

00:03:11.116 --> 00:03:13.611
We think that we live in
a post-feminist society,

00:03:13.611 --> 00:03:15.155
and we do not.

00:03:15.155 --> 00:03:18.315
So we're told we don't
need feminism anymore,

00:03:18.315 --> 00:03:20.735
that we have the vote,
that like we're all good.

00:03:20.735 --> 00:03:23.051
And I think actually that's
incredibly disconcerting

00:03:23.051 --> 00:03:26.189
because then, when young
women move into the world

00:03:26.189 --> 00:03:29.200
and they realize, oh why am
I not being paid the same?

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.800
Why am I being treated differently?

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:32.841
And they start to blame
themselves, because they don't

00:03:32.841 --> 00:03:35.697
understand that they're
part of a historic pattern,

00:03:35.697 --> 00:03:38.122
they're part of a much larger
system which is kind of

00:03:38.122 --> 00:03:39.516
working a little bit against them.

00:03:39.516 --> 00:03:42.433
Um, no, I don't want it to be over!

00:03:43.437 --> 00:03:45.278
Please don't let it be over.

00:03:45.278 --> 00:03:47.982
I never want to leave, I
only want to be into you

00:03:47.982 --> 00:03:49.257
by Buzzfeed from now on.

00:03:49.257 --> 00:03:51.515
I'm really gonna struggle
to say goodbye to this guy.

00:03:51.515 --> 00:03:54.517
Massive shout-out to Best
Friends Animal Society,

00:03:54.517 --> 00:03:58.203
who save hundreds, and hundreds,
and hundreds of kittens.

00:03:58.203 --> 00:04:00.780
They make sure that
these guys find a home.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:02.584
This has been the
highlight of my press tour,

00:04:02.584 --> 00:04:03.417
without a doubt.

00:04:03.417 --> 00:04:04.479
We're peaking right now.

00:04:04.479 --> 00:04:06.299
There's nothing that's gonna top this.

00:04:06.299 --> 00:04:08.333
(light music)

